1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,120
I was thinking about the client's
feedback all night.

2
00:00:03,634 --> 00:00:07,554
Me too, and I'm thinking about changing
the whole color palette.

3
00:00:08,026 --> 00:00:10,026
I think that's a smart move.

4
00:00:10,511 --> 00:00:13,391
The orange looks too loud next to their
logo.

5
00:00:13,832 --> 00:00:16,952
Do you think the client will accept a
darker blue?

6
00:00:17,388 --> 00:00:20,348
I think so, if we keep enough contrast.

7
00:00:20,839 --> 00:00:24,439
Why do you think he left the meeting so
early yesterday?

8
00:00:24,891 --> 00:00:28,251
I think he was angry about the wrong font
on the cover.

9
00:00:28,577 --> 00:00:30,977
Wait, which font was wrong?

10
00:00:31,428 --> 00:00:35,268
Our intern sent the old draft, not the
final mockup.

11
00:00:35,637 --> 00:00:39,957
Hold on, Sara, I thought you checked the
files before the meeting.

12
00:00:40,421 --> 00:00:44,101
I did, but I didn't think she had
replaced them afterwards.

13
00:00:44,525 --> 00:00:48,045
I don't think she knew which version was
the final one.

14
00:00:48,499 --> 00:00:52,099
Maybe, but I don't think the client cares
about that.

15
00:00:52,656 --> 00:00:54,976
Don't you think we should call him today?

16
00:00:55,376 --> 00:00:56,816
I don't think so.

17
00:00:57,155 --> 00:01:00,035
He only wants a new presentation by
Friday.

18
00:01:00,423 --> 00:01:04,183
That's tight, because the layout needs a
lot of work.

19
00:01:04,684 --> 00:01:07,804
At first, I didn't think we would finish
in time.

20
00:01:08,292 --> 00:01:12,372
When we got the brief, I didn't think the
client was so demanding.

21
00:01:12,762 --> 00:01:16,522
Neither did I, because he seemed very
relaxed that day.

22
00:01:16,945 --> 00:01:20,865
By the way, I'm not thinking about
redesigning the logo.

23
00:01:21,337 --> 00:01:23,897
I don't think the logo is the problem.

24
00:01:24,344 --> 00:01:28,424
Right, the real problem is too little
white space.

25
00:01:28,919 --> 00:01:33,079
Okay, Tom, you can fix the layout, and
I'll do the colors.

26
00:01:33,441 --> 00:01:36,801
Should we ask the intern to help with the
mockups?

27
00:01:37,232 --> 00:01:41,072
Yes, because I don't think she'll make
the same mistake again.

28
00:01:41,441 --> 00:01:44,321
I think she learned a big lesson
yesterday.

29
00:01:44,866 --> 00:01:48,786
Great, let's send the new version to the
client by Thursday night.

30
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:53,310
Perfect, and this time I'll check every
file twice.

